text I'm standing on a piece of earth as the wind howls by me.
text It feels as though it's blowing from the edge of the world, with nothing standing in its way.
text Even this body of mine can feel its strength.
text Countless lights dance on the earth, as if stirred by the wind.
text A girl is standing among them.
text They're stirred again, and many of the lights leap up from the ground.
text The girl looks up at them.
text This is the world I was born into.
text I think about how... illusionary it is.
text Trees, grass, stones that roll by me; they all seem completely natural.
text They're supposed to be here.
text But what are the lights?
text I'm sure I hadn't known about this spectacle for a long time.
text The wind picks up again, and one of the lights passes by me.
text I try chasing after it.
text It's floating there, right within arm's length.
text I reach out to it.
text The light slips through my fingers of junk.
text It's not like they'd be able to change anything even if they COULD grab hold of it.
text I stand there dumbfounded; the sight of the girl's shadow tells me that she's by my side, though.
text I point at one of the lights.
text ..."What is it?" the girl asks.
text I'm unable to answer.
text ..."Does that light seem strange?"
text I nod.
text ..."What about the sky?"
text I shake my head no.
text ..."The ground?"
text No.
text ..."Just this light?"
text Nod.
text ..."Why could that be?"
text The girl puts a hand to her chin as she thinks.
text I try to do the same, but the joints on my elbow don't bend that far.
text So I wait there, my arm bent unnaturally.
text She's always lived here. The light must be no different to her than my impression of the water and the trees.
text They're a part of nature.
text But they're the one thing I can't touch.
text Which makes me think... that they must be shadows.
text But shadows are all cast by something, right?
text So where could that thing be...?
text I look, but it's nowhere to be found.
text ..."So that means," the girl begins...
text ..."If we're able to think of something as strange, we know what normal looks like."
text Perhaps. I nod.
